core 4: degree-4 neighbor sets endpoint-compatible 5985/5985; degree-5 sets 20349/20349
core 5: degree-4 neighbor sets endpoint-compatible 5985/5985; degree-5 sets 20349/20349

Interpretation:
- In all five exact graph6 cores, every vertex can be a Hamiltonian endpoint.
- For every existing vertex v, every incident edge can serve as the reattachment
  edge after deleting v; endpoint-options hist equals degree hist.
- Therefore any positive-degree graph-only one-vertex extension of a 57-edge
  core remains traceable by attaching the new vertex to a core endpoint.
- So traceability/unit-spine arguments cannot prove u(22)<=60 by themselves.
- The proof must forbid a realizable unit-cocyclic degree-4 neighbor set over
  the five 57-edge cores, or else use the totally-unfaithful obstruction library.

